\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Pointwise residuals between the normalised frFFT density and the analytical Gaussian density, evaluated at the active fine-grid points within $\pm 5\sigma $ of each trajectory's mean. The vertical axes carry exponents of $10^{-14}$ (trajectory 0) and $10^{-15}$ (trajectories 1--3), confirming that the residuals are at the level of double-precision machine epsilon. The oscillatory, zero-mean pattern is characteristic of floating-point rounding noise with no systematic bias.}}{60}{figure.5.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frfft_residuals}{{5.1}{60}{Pointwise residuals between the normalised frFFT density and the analytical Gaussian density, evaluated at the active fine-grid points within $\pm 5\sigma $ of each trajectory's mean. The vertical axes carry exponents of $10^{-14}$ (trajectory 0) and $10^{-15}$ (trajectories 1--3), confirming that the residuals are at the level of double-precision machine epsilon. The oscillatory, zero-mean pattern is characteristic of floating-point rounding noise with no systematic bias}{figure.5.1}{}}
